## What is `package.json`

`package.json` is the manifest file for a Node.js / npm project. It defines the project's metadata, dependencies, and scripts. npm reads it to understand how to build, test, and run the project.

## Common top-level keys

| Key | Meaning |
|-----|---------|
| **`name`** | The project's name. Must be lowercase, URL-safe (no spaces or uppercase). This is the name published to the npm registry. |
| **`version`** | The project version, following **Semantic Versioning** (major.minor.patch), e.g. `1.0.0`. |
| **`description`** | A one-line human-readable description of the project. |
| **`scripts`** | A map of named commands runnable via `npm run <name>`. Common ones: `test`, `start`, `build`, `dev`, `lint`. |
| **`main`** | The entry point of the module (e.g., `index.js` or `dist/index.js`). Used when something does `require('./your-package')`. |
| **`type`** | Sets the JS module system: `"module"` (ESM) or `"commonjs"` (default). Affects how `.js` files are interpreted. |
| **`keywords`** | An array of strings used to help users find the package on the npm registry. |
| **`author`** | The package author (can be a string or an object with name/email/homepage). |
| **`license`** | The license term (e.g., `"MIT"`, `"ISC"`, `"GPL-3.0"`), governing how others may use the code. |
| **`dependencies`** | Runtime dependencies required for the package to run. Installed into `node_modules` on `npm install`. |
| **`devDependencies`** | Dependencies needed only for development/testing/build (e.g., `jest`, `eslint`, `webpack`). Not needed in production. |
| **`engines`** | Declares supported Node.js (and optionally npm) versions, e.g. `"node": ">=18.0.0"`. |
| **`repository`** | The source repo location (type + URL), so the published package links back to its source. |
| **`homepage`** | URL to the project's homepage/docs. |
| **`bugs`** | URL or object pointing to the issue tracker. |
| **`files`** | An allow-list of files included when the package is published (e.g., `["dist", "README.md"]`). |
| **`publishConfig`** | Overrides for the publish behavior (e.g., default registry, access level). |
| **`bin`** | Declares executable command(s) to expose when the package is installed globally. |
| **`config`** | Default configuration values that can be read by the package at runtime via `process.config`. |
| **`peerDependencies`** | Packages that must be installed by the *consumer* of your package (e.g., a React plugin that needs peer React). |

## Files that commonly accompany it
- **`node_modules/`** — installed dependencies (generated, usually not committed).
- **`package-lock.json`** — a lockfile pinning exact dependency versions for reproducible installs.

